    "media:imagetext": "Confidential\netter Nor 197-37\nSeptember 17, 1937\nMr. H. M. Bixby\nVice President for China\nPan American Airways Co.\nManila, Philippine Islands\nDear Mr. Bixby:\nI enclose for your information and files copy of a memo-\nrandum dated September 8th which I have prepared here and which is\nself-explanatory.\nThe memorandum attached thereto and dated August\n25th is, as you will imediately perceive, a synthetic composition of\nyour memorandum of August 25th and your personal and confidential let-\nter of the same date, but with certain confidential, off-the-record,\nand imaterial matter omnitted. My object was to have one memorandum\ngiving the record of the events leading up to your departure fron Chine\nwhich would be in such form that it could be show to any interested\nparties and form,\n1l necessary, a part of a published or legal record.\nI believe this memorandum will fill the purpose I have in mind but if\nyou have any conments to make, and particularly if you have any addi-\ntions to incorporate, I would appreciate having them in the form of a\nsupplementary memorandum with no confidential material included which\ncould be attached to this as a part of the official record.\nThe mail was just received today with your letters B-1 to\nB-21, ommitting B-2 and B-6 not received, and gives us more infornation\nand a good deal of interesting comment but nothing which I think has to\nbe added.\nThe President has instructed me, with the Comptroller, to\nprepare a statement showing as nearly as poseible the actual losses euf-\nfered through our forced withdrawl fron China.\nI find our last CNAC\nstatement is that for May and I do not suppose that a later statement\nwill be received. If you have or can obtain any data tending to reflect\nthe belance sheet for CNAC at a later date than that, we should like to\nhave it.\nWith regard to our PAA losses, we are having Mr. Nowlin prepare\na statement of all property in China fully owned by Pan Americen Airways\nIl at a ister date any of\nthis property can be salvaged it can, of course, be checked off on this\nlist. I do not know in what manner we will present our claim for our\nfair participation in the assets of CNAC at the time of our withdrawal,\nor for Losses Butterb (gaie shall probably consult with",
